# Test: dataplane drift command, live bad-packet wire capture (`show system bad-packets`), `show firewall trace` RPC wiring, `request support archive` live runtime modules (`internal/core/supportreg` on both local and daemon routes), live MCP `ze://triage` resource (`ttlMs: 5000`), and `doctor-dataplane-drift` work end-to-end on a live daemon.
# QUESTION: on a live `ze start` daemon, does `show system drift` return structured JSON and refuse unknown `| subsystem <name>`, does sending a corrupt BGP header over TCP populate `show system bad-packets`, `show system bad-packets | protocol bgp`, `show system triage` `runtime.bad-packet-count`, and MCP `resources/read` (`ze://triage`, `ttlMs: 5000`, `cacheScope: "private"`), does `show firewall trace` route through YANG dispatch, does daemon-routed `request support archive` via MCP collect all 10 live runtime modules (7 core + 3 daemon-backed `event-ring`, `plugins`, `reload-history`) while local `ze request support archive` collects the 7 core modules, and is `doctor-dataplane-drift` explainable via `ze show diagnostic`?
# A unit test cannot decide this because the path spans live `ze start` daemon startup (`Server.StartWithContext` registering drift remote collectors and daemon live support modules), real TCP BGP ingress header rejection into `internal/core/badpacket`, SSH CLI dispatch with command-owned `| subsystem` and `| protocol` pipes, live HTTP MCP `resources/list` + `resources/read` (`ze://triage`) + `tools/call` daemon-routed support archive collection, and local support archive collection.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-ai-diagnostics-5-drift-explain-and-support-registry AC-1, AC-2, AC-3, AC-4, AC-6, AC-7, AC-8.
# PREVENTS: unwired `Server.StartWithContext` drift/support registration, broken BGP cold-path bad-packet recording on live TCP reads, broken `| subsystem`/`| protocol` CLI pipe filters, broken MCP `ze://triage` live-state caching/dispatch, or missing live support modules on daemon or local routes.

